// Same-step guard compensation with an ANCHOR-SHARED correlation var — the
// sibling of the 0904 family's same-step case in which the correlation
// variable is bound by the anchor rather than by the request.
//
// `Heartbeat{server: x} since Login{server: x}` requires an UNBROKEN
// per-server heartbeat streak since that server's login. An implementation
// may key the guard streak per server correctly and still get this wrong, if
// its check for "the guard fires NOW" tests only the guard's predicate SHAPE
// and not that the event's `server` matches the anchor being validated.
//
// @30 is the trap: server s1's streak is alive through @20, and a heartbeat
// fires at @30 — but for server s2. An unconstrained same-step check wrongly
// extends s1's streak → over-PERMIT. The correct verdict is DENY: s1's streak
// broke at @30, and s2 has no Login anchor. @10/@20 are the over-constraint
// controls — a MATCHING same-step heartbeat must keep permitting.
//
// Expected verdicts are in expected_1.out.
permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Heartbeat",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    exists (x: String). (
        Drupe::Action::"Heartbeat"::request{ input.server: x }
        since within 1h
        Drupe::Action::"Login"::request{ input.server: x }
    )
};
